{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"c7dd90e3ce4a3fd3","name":"card_unit_13_gebirgsjager","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Germany/WinterWar/units/card_unit_13_gebirgsjager","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"13. GEBIRGSJÄGER","text":"Gets +1+1 when you add or deploy an Alpine unit.","flavorText":"The 13th Gebirgsjäger-Regiment was a unit of the 4th Mountain Division of the German Wehrmacht during WWII. The division was activated in October 1940, and in 1941 it participated in the Balkans Campaign, before joining Army Group South in Operation Barbarossa, the German invasion of the Soviet Union. In 1942 the division took part in Operation Edelweiss, which was a failed German offensive that aimed at securing the oil fields in the Caucasus, particularly in Baku. This was done to meet Germany's growing fuel needs and to cut off a crucial supply for the Soviet Union. Following the operation’s failure, the division was on the defensive and pushed back, first to the Crimean Peninsula, Ukraine, then to Hungary, Slovakia, and finally it surrendered to the Red Army in May 1945 near the Czech city of Olomouc.","faction":"Germany","type":"infantry","rarity":"Common","cost":3,"operationCost":1,"attack":2,"defense":3},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_unit_13_gebirgsjager","title":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_13_gebirgsjager_title","SourceString":"13. GEBIRGSJÄGER","LocalizedString":"13. GEBIRGSJÄGER"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::infantry","attack":2,"defense":3,"range":1,"faction":"EFactionEnum::Germany","kredits":3,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_13_gebirgsjager_text","SourceString":"Gets +1+1 when you add or deploy an Alpine unit.","LocalizedString":"Gets +1+1 when you add or deploy an Alpine unit."},"flavorText":{"Namespace":"card_germany","Key":"card_unit_13_gebirgsjager_history","SourceString":"The 13th Gebirgsjäger-Regiment was a unit of the 4th Mountain Division of the German Wehrmacht during WWII. The division was activated in October 1940, and in 1941 it participated in the Balkans Campaign, before joining Army Group South in Operation Barbarossa, the German invasion of the Soviet Union. In 1942 the division took part in Operation Edelweiss, which was a failed German offensive that aimed at securing the oil fields in the Caucasus, particularly in Baku. This was done to meet Germany's growing fuel needs and to cut off a crucial supply for the Soviet Union. Following the operation’s failure, the division was on the defensive and pushed back, first to the Crimean Peninsula, Ukraine, then to Hungary, Slovakia, and finally it surrendered to the Red Army in May 1945 near the Czech city of Olomouc.","LocalizedString":"The 13th Gebirgsjäger-Regiment was a unit of the 4th Mountain Division of the German Wehrmacht during WWII. The division was activated in October 1940, and in 1941 it participated in the Balkans Campaign, before joining Army Group South in Operation Barbarossa, the German invasion of the Soviet Union. In 1942 the division took part in Operation Edelweiss, which was a failed German offensive that aimed at securing the oil fields in the Caucasus, particularly in Baku. This was done to meet Germany's growing fuel needs and to cut off a crucial supply for the Soviet Union. Following the operation’s failure, the division was on the defensive and pushed back, first to the Crimean Peninsula, Ukraine, then to Hungary, Slovakia, and finally it surrendered to the Red Army in May 1945 near the Czech city of Olomouc."},"operationCost":1,"rarity":"ERarityEnum::Common","cardSet":"ECardSetEnum::WinterWar","isReserved":true,"EffectType":"ECardEffectTypes::Trigger","usedTriggers":["ERegisteredCardFunction::OnOtherCardEnterPlay"],"extraHelpTextBubbleTypes":["EHelpBubbleTypes::Alpine","EHelpBubbleTypes::Trigger"],"hasAlpine":true,"Image":{"AssetPathName":"/Game/Assets/Textures/Images/Germany/CandidateArtwork/Winter_War/t_winter_germans_b.t_winter_germans_b","SubPathString":""},